WEBVTT

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.000
We'll be fine.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.250
Because we've practiced...

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.790
...more than anyone for sure!

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.330
You'll be fine.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.250
You survived my tough lessons.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.950
Don't forget.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.540
What's important isn't
going to nationals itself,

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.830
but <i>why </i>you want to go to nationals.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:38.080
So to them, it's their last chance.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.200
I don't want it to end yet.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.370
I wish it could go on forever.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.870
Next year won't work for you guys!

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.830
Next year... will be too late.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.750
We're gonna go to nationals for sure!

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:26.870
"#25    Tenkyu"

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.120
I can't believe it! What kind
of performance is that?!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.120
It's evenly matched with ours...
though how it was done was quite different...

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.040
Judges' votes will probably be split, too.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.870
What's with these high-level performances...?
What's happening?

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.830
Himesaka and Hakuto...
Only one of them can go to nationals...?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.120
You gotta be kidding me...!

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.370
It was amazing...

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.330
It's like Hakuto was amazing in a totally
different way than Himesaka.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:03.660
Yeah... they were... I bet the judges
are gonna have a hard time deciding.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.500
With music, how do they
decide which one's better?

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.700
The difficulty and degree
of perfection of the piece?

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.790
Yeah, they're important. But when schools
are at the same level for both,

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.700
I think it'll depend on
what each judge values...

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.330
Do they value an aesthetic of staying together?

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.330
Or do they value how
the sound was expressed?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.540
Honey! Takezo and the others
are taking the stage!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.580
I wonder if he'll be okay?
He often makes mistakes at critical times.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.290
Calm down, dear.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.120
Good, Granny. We made it back just in time.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.540
Yeah.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.200
Takezo...! Everyone...! Go for it!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.870
This isn't like me. I'm getting kinda nervous.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.040
They'll be fine...

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.660
...since they've practiced like crazy.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.750
Mr. Tsukaji!

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.950
The next school has five boys! This is amazing!

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.120
To think that they're playing
after Hakuto... I feel bad for them.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.120
Honestly, I don't even want to hear
the crappy performances coming up.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.790
It's likely that either Himesaka
or Hakuto will win anyway...

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.250
Tokise...

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:00.160
Program number 13.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.040
Tokise High School.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.790
"Tenkyu."

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:31.040
The words I repeated
so many times in my head...

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.540
Your koto... is like a weapon to me.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:43.910
How pathetic... that I'm afraid of hearing
my own daughter's performance...

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:49.120
I never understood it. I couldn't face it.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.660
But now...

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.040
Ahh... That's right. This is it.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.620
This is completely different from that time.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.500
A single note...

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.540
I have to work hard, too.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:57.040
So that you can always
have a smile on your face.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.290
How can she play...

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.700
...a sound like this...?

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.200
Satowa...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.410
She's already in a class of her own.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:16.160
But there's no way that
the others can match her sound!

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:39.290
Is this really possible...?!

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.910
This can't be happening...
Those vulgar delinquents can...?

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:47.750
You're not worthy to play
the koto with Satowa!

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:02.160
If you consider the 17-string and the solo
as the "root" and "trunk" of a tree...

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:06.620
...the first and second kotos are leaves
and blossoms that lend colors to it.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.870
Hold on a sec...

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:34.250
What the heck is going on?! This sound...!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.290
It's not just the solo part...?!

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.790
Their sound is completely different
from the other schools.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:03.410
The care they put into each note...
How it resonates... The others are no match.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:46.250
Who are these kids...?
How did they become like this?

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.330
Just how much time...
did they spend practicing?!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:04.040
I liked your performance.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.750
It was a good performance.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.160
You guys can become even better.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.580
So I don't want the next
competition to be our last.

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:25.660
With those guys... I'll give it everything
I've got until the very end.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:31.160
I wanna get better as soon as possible.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:35.120
There are things we need
to do before we complain!

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.370
That sound is your soul itself.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.830
It's your soul itself.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:05.120
After suddenly losing someone precious to me,

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:09.330
I had to protect that which was left behind.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:13.620
I thought I could somehow
manage it... and overcome it...

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.080
...because I had my daughter.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:21.580
But I was weak.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:25.950
I was weaker... a lot weaker than I thought...

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.870
...that I let go of...

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.500
...the only light I had.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.410
I thought I'd quit...

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:39.290
I thought there was no point in playing
the koto anymore if I couldn't help Mom.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.410
But...

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.620
The theme moves from part
to part every two beats!

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.290
High-level techniques are used
at important spots.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.410
But they play in a way
that we pay no attention to them

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.160
by completely hiding the difficulty
of their performance.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.870
That's how music should be.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.660
The highlight scene
for each part is starting now.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:26.000
Oh... I'm so happy...

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.620
I'm having so much fun!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.540
I want to play... a lot, lot while longer...
with these guys...

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.540
You could just play alone.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.830
The sound you get when you play
with friends you've spent time with...

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.950
You just can't produce it on your own.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.250
You're damn right, Granddad.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.330
I understand it now.

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:50.000
Good. Now, the last part.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.410
Hm?

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:03.370
O-Oh...? We finished, but...

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.830
No applause...?!

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.870
W-Was something weird...?!

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.870
Guys! It's blacked out,
so take your koto and leave the stage!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.160
O-Okay.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.790
N-Now?!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:07.870
The applause started at
a weird time, didn't it?

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.660
Yeah, it happened after the blackout.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:13.370
I wonder if our performance
wasn't that good...

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.870
No way!

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:18.250
I think our performance today
was the best one ever.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.370
Takezo...!

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:23.540
Everyone! Good job!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.910
Miss Aki!

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.790
Mr. Suzu!

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:31.700
Was our performance bad?! How was it?!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.750
Please be honest!

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:42.200
Why are you... looking so worried...

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.540
...after giving such a wonderful performance?

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:50.750
Right, Mr. Takinami?

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.450
Yeah. It was so-so.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:55.620
Now, get a move on already.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.620
So it wasn't that good after all!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.830
Takinami, you bastard!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:06.500
Mr. Takinami! You're stubborn.
You should be honest and say--

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.580
I'm always honest.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:12.160
Having watched them
all this time, it's obvious

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.870
a performance like that is
nothing special for them.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.660
Hozy. Is something wrong?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:30.250
Oh, no... I just feel kinda listless
now that we're done...

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:32.580
Oh, yeah. Me, too.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:38.750
But now, we just have to wait for
the results, huh?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:40.160
Yeah.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.750
Dammit! Dammit!
Tokise High School was good!

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.200
I cried, too!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.500
I'm scared! What's going on? Why?

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:55.080
"Dazed..."

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:58.830
It was... a very good performance.

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:02.500
Not just performance,
but the piece was incredible.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.000
I created my piece in a way
that allowed Kanzaki to stand out

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:08.290
and balanced his role with the others.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.750
In contrast, Tokise's piece was constructed

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:14.660
to make sure to bring out
the characteristics of each part.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:19.120
Dammit... Today is the last day for me...

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.950
...and yet, I'm already itching
to write the next piece.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.750
Takaoka... I need more tissues.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.700
Well, mine's all gone, too. Seriously,
how much do you have to cry?

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:32.700
What?!

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.870
Hey, are you okay?!

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.000
I-I'm sorry. I'm just so deeply moved...

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.250
Takaoka. Give her some tissues.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.370
Like I said, mine's all gone!

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.450
"Service Entrance"

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:50.450
Well then, kids, good work today.
It was a good performance.

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:52.330
Thanks, Granny!

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.660
Thank you very much!

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:58.040
Okay, then. All the performances
are finished now,

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:01.120
and there's some time before
the results are announced.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.500
What're you guys gonna do?
Just head to the hall?

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:05.830
Well, I don't know.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.410
I'm thirsty.

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.700
Oh, then let's go buy something to--

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:14.290
U-Um, I'm sorry, but can I
step out for a moment?!

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:17.450
I-It looks like my mother came
to hear our performance, so...

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:22.080
Um... Sh-She may've gone home,
but just in case...

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.830
I'm sorry. I know this is personal--

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.870
Why didn't you say so sooner?!

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.830
He's right, Hozy!

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:38.290
You should've just let us
take care of your koto! Jeez...!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:41.700
Hozuki's mom! Please still be around!

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.540
Sorry! We'll all go and help her!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:47.540
What? Do they all have to go, too?

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.160
Mr. Takinami...

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.330
We should go, too!

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.250
Huh?

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:00.080
Okay! We're gonna split up and find her!

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:03.160
What? You know what Hozy's
mom's face looks like, Chika?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.790
No! But I should find a
grand-master-looking person, right?!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:07.620
What?!

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.410
Sh-She's wearing a kimono.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.080
That's it!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:18.410
Guys! If you find her, ask her
to stay and contact Hozuki!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.120
Text or call Hozy!

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.370
If I remember correctly,
she was sitting around here...

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:44.120
Dammit! I hope she's still around...

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.580
I can't find her... Maybe she really is--

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.790
"Hiro"
"Sorry, Hozy.
I couldn't find her over here."

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.370
The only place we haven't
looked is backstage...

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.410
What... am I doing...?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.870
There's no way she'd come here...
when she's got no business here.

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:48.290
What did I expect...?

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:51.160
Satowa...

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:51.950
Next time, "Starting Line."

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:54.540
"#26    Starting Line"
